<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippines' two-month budget gap 3.55 bln.</title>
<headline>Philippines' two-month budget gap 3.55 bln.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippines posted a budget deficit of 3.55 billion pesos for the first two months of 1997, down from a deficit of 5.73 billion pesos a year ago, the Bureau of Treasury said on Thursday.</p>
<p>    FISCAL DEFICIT	 Jan-Feb 97     Jan-Feb 96</p>
<p>(in billion pesos)</p>
<p>    Revenues		  64.156	    62.226</p>
<p>    Expenditures	    67.706	    67.956</p>
<p>    Deficit		    3.550	     5.730</p>
<p>The 1997 figures are preliminary, the Treasury said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Manila newsroom (632) 841 8937</p>
</text>
